{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AW7C5NayNVjZHk5zTVWY5C","type":"tool_result","content":"448:Cluster DNS is the honest illustration. It is, formally, an addon: a cluster extension, not a control-plane or node component. In practice almost every real cluster has it, because Services are addressed by name and Pods expect to be able to resolve those names.\n488:*Every arrow terminates at the API server, and only the API server reaches etcd. Now look for the arrows that aren't drawn: none from the scheduler to a kubelet, none between the two nodes, none from anything but the API server to the datastore. What's missing here is the point of the figure.*\n570:- **A is wrong** — addons are entirely production-appropriate. Cluster DNS in particular is present in essentially every working cluster.\n577:- **D is wrong** — components don't reach past the API server into etcd. The API server is the front end for the control plane, and that phrase means what it sounds like.\n584:✓ The hub arrangement: everything through the API server, only the API server to etcd"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"96dd717d-ea66-42ea-8350-ffb69bfc0340","uuid":"016f0017-1812-46ac-a838-3f05e0f247e2","timestamp":"2026-08-24T07:27:21.879Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"448:Cluster DNS is the honest illustration. It is, formally, an addon: a cluster extension, not a control-plane or node component. In practice almost every real cluster has it, because Services are addressed by name and Pods expect to be able to resolve those names.\n488:*Every arrow terminates at the API server, and only the API server reaches etcd. Now look for the arrows that aren't drawn: none from the scheduler to a kubelet, none between the two nodes, none from anything but the API server to the datastore. What's missing here is the point of the figure.*\n570:- **A is wrong** — addons are entirely production-appropriate. Cluster DNS in particular is present in essentially every working cluster.\n577:- **D is wrong** — components don't reach past the API server into etcd. The API server is the front end for the control plane, and that phrase means what it sounds like.\n584:✓ The hub arrangement: everything through the API server, only the API server to etcd","numLines":5,"totalLines":5}}
